  "notes": "Source: official UCR Bourns College of Engineering (BCOE) Student Affairs 'Suggested Course Plan for a UC Riverside Major in COMPUTER SCIENCE, Catalog Year: 2019' (student.engr.ucr.edu). Transcription method: PDF text extraction of the official term-by-term table, verified line-by-line against the downloaded document; quarter-by-quarter unit sums (13/16/12/17/18/13/16/14/12/16/16/12) add to the plan's stated Total Units: 175 (quarter units; UCR is on the quarter system). Caveats: (1) This 2019 catalog-year plan is the LATEST official term-by-term sample plan UCR publishes for the plain BS Computer Science program as of 2026-09-30; exhaustive searches of catalog.ucr.edu, cs.ucr.edu, engr.ucr.edu, and student.engr.ucr.edu found no 2020+ suggested course plan for plain CS (only the separate Data Science program has a 2024 plan). (2) Course numbering follows the 2019 plan (CS 010/012/014); later catalogs renumbered these to CS 010A/010B/010C. (3) Breadth slots are student-choice courses from the approved BCOE breadth list (Humanities 3 / Social Sciences 3 / Natural Sciences 4 areas, one course covering the biological-science requirement via BIOL 002, 003, or 005A/LA); exact courses not specified by the source. (4) Seven technical-elective slots (28+ units, at least 4 from Computer Science courses) are student-choice from the plan's approved technical-elective list. (5) The source lists no course-by-course prerequisites, so prereq arrays are empty per the no-invention rule; students must consult catalog.ucr.edu for actual prerequisites. (6) ENGR 180W (Technical Communications) fulfills the third quarter of the English composition requirement per the source. (7) The plan notes 'Course Plan is subject to change' and caps at 220 maximum units.",
